- skills/memory/SKILL.md (+ .codex mirror): description said "three backends
  (local, kernel, opt-in Graphiti)" while the body/router say TWO public
  backends. Corrected to "two public backends (local default, opt-in Graphiti;
  kernel internal-only)" so an agent can't be led to set memory.backend: kernel.
- docs/guides/memory-backends.md: MCP wiring is a FAST-FOLLOW, not present-tense.
  Fixed "wires the MCP server into your .mcp.json" and "Turning it off → delete
  the entry" to say Forge does not write one yet; annotated the config block so
  reserved (no-op-until-renderer) keys are marked distinct from active ones.
- lib/memory/graphiti-mcp.js: DEFAULTS now document which keys are CONSUMED vs
  RESERVED (dbUri/neo4jUri/llmProvider/model/groupId have no effect until the
  fast-follow renderer).
- lib/memory/router.js: fireAndForgetGraphitiEmit gains a CONTRACT comment — any
  future emitter MUST bound its own timeout and unref()/leave no lingering handle
  so it can never keep the event loop alive or stall CLI exit.
- test/commands/doctor-memory.test.js: add a case locking non-fatality
  (report.ok stays true when the memory check reports a problem).

